Z||000002||Patrick86GT||10-16-2001||06:34 PM||||I recall reading that GM had designed and outfitted PS for the fiero, but refused to equip any cars due to "noise" generated by the system in test cars.<P>Out of curiosity, why would you want it? In my experience (many fieros), they are easy to steer! ||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnF||10-16-2001||06:56 PM||||The answer to "How do you get power steering?" is like all other answers - SPEND MONEY!<P>No, GM did not install such item, some dealers however, did.  There are a few Fieros running around out there with power steering.<P>Power steering systems can be had - for the right amount of money.  They are powered electrically instead of hydraulically as on other cars.<P>||||reg||10
Z||000004||Kasdan||10-16-2001||07:18 PM||||Excuse me?  electrically?  funny, mines not!  i saw the rack for the first time today, VERY intresting what i saw....||||reg||1
Z||000005||Old Lar||10-16-2001||07:26 PM||||A Mercury Mekur hydraulic power steering unit can be retrofitted to a Fiero, if you can find a Mercury Merkur.  Spend money as stated above.||||reg||1
